  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "VXLAN: Add VNI and Group Policy ID in the tree item",
  "description": "Currently the VXLAN tree item only shows plain protocol name:\n\n```\n...\nEthernet II, Src: LCFCElectron_f8:35:a2 (00:2b:67:f8:35:a2), Dst: MicroStarInt_40:44:19 (d4:3d:7e:40:44:19)\nInternet Protocol Version 4, Src: 192.168.16.4, Dst: 192.168.16.1\nUser Datagram Protocol, Src Port: 42121, Dst Port: 4789\nVirtual eXtensible Local Area Network\nEthernet II, Src: ProxmoxServe_11:11:11 (bc:24:11:11:11:11), Dst: Broadcast (ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff)\n...\n```\n\nThis adds the VNI and Group Policy ID in the tree item, removing the need to expand the VXLAN subtree to see the values:\n\n```\n...\nEthernet II, Src: LCFCElectron_f8:35:a2 (00:2b:67:f8:35:a2), Dst: MicroStarInt_40:44:19 (d4:3d:7e:40:44:19)\nInternet Protocol Version 4, Src: 192.168.16.4, Dst: 192.168.16.1\nUser Datagram Protocol, Src Port: 42121, Dst Port: 4789\nVirtual eXtensible Local Area Network, VNI: 5001, GP ID: 0\nEthernet II, Src: ProxmoxServe_11:11:11 (bc:24:11:11:11:11), Dst: Broadcast (ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff)\n...\n```\n\nSample capture file: [vxlan.pcapng](/uploads/22186294c2bccb31f363bac18efb05c2/vxlan.pcapng)\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
